  "question": {
    "text": "A seconds pendulum clock having steel wire is calibrated at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>20</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mo>°</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math>. When temperature is increased to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>30</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mo>°</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math>, then calculate how much time does the clock lose or gain in one week&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mtext>steel</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mtext>.</mtext><mn>2</mn><mo>×</mo><mn>1</mn><msup><mn>0</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&nbsp;</mo><msup><mspace></mspace><mo>∘</mo></msup><msup><mtext>C</mtext><mn>-1</mn></msup></mrow></mfenced></math>",
